/* Prototype of genmessages.c's dumpHelp() retargeted to Doxygen syntax, instead
 * of halibut syntax. Real dumpHelp() emits ONE \S{key} block per message into
 * ONE stream (messages.but) -- this mirrors that exact structure with \page
 * blocks instead, one per message, all in this one file. Confirmed via a
 * throwaway test that \page (unlike a markdown "# heading {#anchor}") DOES
 * produce a separate output page per block even when several appear in one
 * input file -- so, unlike an earlier (wrong) conclusion in this
 * investigation, genmessages.c does NOT need restructuring to write one file
 * per message; only the per-message emitted syntax changes.
 *
 * Just 2 of the real 130 messages.in entries, for the SF #220-adjacent
 * Halibut -> Doxygen proof-of-concept (see
 * .claude/halibut-doxygen-investigation-plan.md).
 */

